<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patrick Henry</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1736">1736</a>–<a href="/years/1799">1799</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patrick Henry was a Virginian lawyer and orator who became a leading voice of resistance to British rule. He opposed the Stamp Act in 1765 and in 1775 urged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> to arm with the words 'Give me liberty, or give me death!'. He served as the first governor of the independent state of Virginia and later opposed the federal Constitution as a threat to the rights of the states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patrick-henry.jpg" alt="Patrick Henry" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Bagby Matthews (1857 - 1943), after Thomas Sully (1783-1872) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patrick_henry.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
